<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pope Adrian I</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Adrian I</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Pope Adrian I was <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishop</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> from 772 to 795. Threatened by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-lombards">Lombards</a>, he appealed to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charlemagne">Charlemagne</a> for help. Charlemagne crossed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alps">Alps</a>, deposed King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/desiderius">Desiderius</a> and absorbed the Lombard kingdom in 774, strengthening the alliance between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/papacy">papacy</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carolingian-empire">Carolingian Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pope-adrian-i.jpg" alt="Pope Adrian I" width="320" height="326" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Francesco Bini · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Zecca_di_roma,_denaro_di_adriano_I,_772-795,_in_argento_(bibl._apostolica_vaticana).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
